.nh
.TH "TAKO" "1" "Jun 2026" "Tako CLI" "Tako CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
tako-preview - List, destroy and prune preview environments


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtako preview [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage preview environments: short-lived copies of a template environment,
one per pull request or branch, created with 'tako deploy --preview \&'.

.PP
See docs/PREVIEW-ENVIRONMENTS.md for template setup, DNS and limits.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for preview


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config file (default is ./tako.yaml or ./tako.json)

.PP
\fB-e\fP, \fB--env\fP=""
	environment to use (default: the only environment, else production, else the first alphabetically)

.PP
\fB--events\fP=""
	stream progress events to stdout: ndjson (human output moves to stderr)

.PP
\fB--host-key-mode\fP=""
	SSH host key verification mode: tofu, strict, ask (default: tofu)

.PP
\fB--output\fP="text"
	output format: text or json (json reserves stdout for the final result document)

.PP
\fB--preview\fP=""
	preview environment to use (deploy, ps, logs, exec, history, rollback, config explain); -e then names its base

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtako(1)\fP, \fBtako-preview-destroy(1)\fP, \fBtako-preview-list(1)\fP, \fBtako-preview-prune(1)\fP
